# DocuMind

RAG document Q&A over Tunisian labor-law PDFs. Read `prd.md` and `docs/architecture.md` before changing pipeline behavior.

## Frozen stack

FastAPI, PyMuPDF, ChromaDB, sentence-transformers, `BAAI/bge-m3`, `BAAI/bge-reranker-base`, Gemini Flash + Ollama fallback, React + Vite + TypeScript, Docker Compose, RAGAS.

Do not add LangChain/LlamaIndex as the orchestrator. Splitters/PDF helpers only if needed.

## Agent behavior

- One module per change. Do not scaffold features from a later phase.
- Never invent legal answers. Low retrieval score → refusal.
- No new dependencies without updating `prd.md` and the matching requirements/package file.
- No secrets in source. Chunk metadata must include `filename` and `page`.
- After RAG config changes, add a row to `docs/decisions.md`.
